    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (82.49) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) as our clear offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a massive park-adjusted xWOBA of 0.476 against Junk, effectively punishing the matchup despite a slight park penalty. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary engine for the scarce stolen base category; his elite sprint speed coupled with a high-upside leadoff spot against Flaherty makes him our most efficient generator of total points. **Christian Yelich** rounds out our top tier (72.79) as the combination of his leadoff positioning and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Peralta cements his status as a must-start despite the neutral park environment.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical tradeoffs in the middle of the order. **Junior Caminero** (56.77) narrowly missed our 60.0 target, squeezed by the elite skill of Cease, whose sub-3.00 xERA caps the upside for even our best hitters. **Pedro Ramirez** (48.06) stands as our most difficult bench decision, trailing the starters due to a lower projected spot in the order, though he remains the first call should any lineup adjustments occur. Conversely, **Colt Keith** (68.41) and **Caleb Durbin** (65.49) are high-confidence starts today; **Caleb Durbin** specifically earns a boost due to a slow opposing delivery that theoretically increases his chances to swipe a base, keeping him ahead of the volatility we see with **Kyle Schwarber** (57.88), who is hampered by a tough matchup against Sheehan.\n\nRisks today are concentrated on the upper-tier arms. While we expect production, we are monitoring the matchups for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**, both of whom draw Sheehan; the SP's ability to suppress production introduces a negative skill adjustment to their base projections. We have confirmed the benching of **Chase Meidroth** (34.47), who falls below our floor due to a brutal draw against deGrom. We remain vigilant on the status of **Gary Sanchez** and **Hyeseong Kim**, who continue to provide no value due to roster and lineup availability, and will keep **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Carson Benge**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** on high alert for any late-breaking substitutions.",
